@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+Local evaluators in most server SDKs treat a property filter with an unrecognized `type` as a person filter. When the flags service adds a filter type, such as `person_metadata`, an SDK that shipped before it compares the filter with a caller-supplied property of the same key and can return a result that disagrees with `/flags`.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Lists the filter types a local evaluator matches, and makes a flag condition with any other type inconclusive with the `unsupported_definition` cause.
+- Leaves a flag with an unknown filter type unresolved instead of requesting it from `/flags`.
+- Keeps every other flag evaluating locally when one flag uses an unknown type.
+- Adds a logging requirement for inconclusive results to the `local-flag-evaluator` spec.
+- Adds acceptance scenarios to `acceptance/private/local-flag-evaluator.feature`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- `local-flag-evaluator`: adds the unknown filter type requirements.
+
+## Impact
+
+posthog-python, posthog-node, and posthog-go treat an unknown filter type as a person filter today and need a change. SDKs that already treat an unknown type as unsupported conform.
